{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-129025",
  "enisaUuid": "4b71adcb-302b-3a36-8910-7ea235e96deb",
  "description": "A vulnerability in Microsoft Compiled HTML Help (CHM) file scanning of ClamAV could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause a DoS condition on an affected device.\r\n\r This vulnerability is due to a logic error when scanning the CHM file and following the internal file pointers. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted CHM file for scanning. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to cause the ClamAV decode process to terminate due to an infinite loop, resulting in a DoS condition on the affected software.",
  "datePublished": "Nov 18, 2026, 4:31:11 PM",
  "dateUpdated": "Nov 18, 2026, 4:46:30 PM",
  "baseScore": 7.5,
  "baseScoreVersion": "3.1",
